{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "N1"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 119, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty edge 3 adds a direct input-to-output path, giving large gains (exps 1,5,7,9), while replacing an existing op is roughly neutral or negative."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the residual skip on edge 3 with a conv removes the identity shortcut and consistently hurts (exps 2,6) in conv-heavy cells."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a residual shortcut where none exists gives larger gains (exps 47,49,52) than swapping it in for a conv (exp 48)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting the identity shortcut hurts more (exps 94,96) than deleting a conv or pool on edge 3 (exps 93,95,100)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 4 is absent, removing edge 5 leaves fewer paths into the output node, which can collapse the cell (exps 14,15 vs 12)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the edge-3 shortcut, edge 5 carries more of the output signal, so removing it is more damaging (exps 11,14)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With no direct input-to-output edge, all signal routes through node 1 or 2, so cutting edge 0 hurts much more (exp 65 vs 61-64)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty edge 5 adds capacity (exp 53), whereas replacing a skip there loses a shortcut and is often negative (exps 54,56,58)."}, 